// ============================================================================
// CommunityLaunch — XelisVault Protocol
// ============================================================================
// The permissionless community-coin factory (the "pump.fun track") for
// XELIS. Where VaultLaunch is the SERIOUS shelf — a community validation
// vote before anything trades, 526 XEL of founder skin in the game, a
// trust system and team vesting — CommunityLaunch is the casino next
// door, and it says so honestly:
//
//   * ANYONE launches a coin, instantly, for ~2 XEL out of pocket
//     (submission fee + the chain's asset-creation cost). No vote, no
//     validation, no founder liquidity required.
//   * The coin is born as a REAL XELIS confidential asset: Asset::create
//     with MaxSupplyMode::Fixed — the WHOLE supply is minted to this
//     contract at launch and can never be increased (the cap is enforced
//     by the XELIS protocol itself, not by our code). Buyers hold real
//     tokens in their own wallets from the first second.
//   * Pricing starts on a VIRTUAL-RESERVE bonding curve (C1): the
//     contract adds a constant virtual XEL reserve (default 100 XEL) and
//     a virtual token reserve equal to the curve's initial inventory to
//     the REAL reserves in every formula. The coin therefore has a
//     sensible price and single-digit-percent slippage from the FIRST
//     buy, with ZERO founder capital — the depth of the book is
//     simulated; only the buyers' real XEL accumulates.
//   * Graduation (C2) fires inside the buy() that crosses it: the REAL
//     reserves must clear the depth floor (default 50 XEL, admin-set,
//     snapshotted per coin) AND the price-continuity condition
//     (xr * y0 >= yr * vx — the real ratio has overtaken the virtual
//     ratio, so the pool the coin migrates into will open at a price at
//     or above the curve's spot: no graduation dump by construction).
//   * The curve keeps trading at the graduated fee until the
//     permissionless migrate() (anyone, any time) moves the curve's
//     whole REAL reserves and REAL inventory into a LaunchDEX pool via
//     the OPEN seeding endpoint (create_pool_open, chunk 33, v1.4) —
//     permissionless on BOTH sides: no pinned signer can become a
//     graduation bottleneck. The pool's seed is protocol-locked FOREVER
//     (LaunchDEX X11) — the community's own money is the anti-rug floor.
//
// The two tracks are SEPARATE BY DESIGN (C3): different contracts,
// different filters, different budgets, different fees — but the same
// DEX lineage (a LaunchDEX generation serves both), the same SDK and
// the same site. The site must never blur them: project tokens earn
// their listing through a community vote; community coins buy their
// launch for 2 XEL. Frontends should label community coins loudly
// ("community coin — no validation") — scams WILL launch here; the
// structural guarantees (fixed supply, no founder liquidity to pull,
// locked pool seed, never-blockable sells) bound what a scam can DO,
// not what a coin can BE.
//
// ANTI-RUG, THE HONEST LIST (what a malicious creator CANNOT do here):
//   * mint past the supply (XELIS enforces the Fixed cap),
//   * pull the launch liquidity (there is none of THEIRS — the pool is
//     seeded with the BUYERS' money, protocol-locked forever, X11),
//   * trap holders (sells carry NO gate — not the pause, not anything;
//     the curve pays out of real reserves that are provably sufficient,
//     IC3/IC4, and the DEX sell path is ungated absolutely, IX6),
//   * honeypot (the curve is the counterparty; the constant-product
//     formula executes the same for every wallet),
//   * reclaim their creator allocation early (it is held OFF the curve
//     and claimable only AFTER migration — a creator's payoff is
//     conditional on the coin graduating).
// What a malicious creator CAN do: dump their 5% creator allocation
// post-migration (public from launch, cap enforced), rug the price with
// a monster sell (their own choice — the pool floor survives), and
// launch a hundred scam coins (each costs the submission fee + an asset
// budget; the site labels them; the moderation key can pause their
// pools' BUYS on the DEX).
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DESIGN DECISIONS (and why — read before changing anything)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// C1. VIRTUAL RESERVES, REAL SOLVENCY. State per coin: xr = real XEL in
//     the curve (starts 0 — the founder provides NOTHING), yr = real
//     curve inventory (starts total_supply - creator allocation), plus
//     two constants snapshotted at launch: vx (virtual XEL, default
//     100 XEL) and y0 (= the initial inventory — so the virtual token
//     reserve always mirrors the real one). Every formula uses the
//     TOTALS: x_total = xr + vx, y_total = yr + y0.
//       buy:  out  = y_total * net / (x_total + net)     (floored)
//       sell: gross = x_total * T / (y_total + T)        (floored)
//     Solvency is not hoped for, it is PROVED (see IC3/IC4): through
//     trades the product k = x_total * y_total never decreases (fees
//     are EXTRACTED to pending_fees, never parked in the reserves;
//     every floor favours the curve), so k >= k0 = vx * 2*y0 forever,
//     and since y_total <= 2*y0 (nothing circulates that was not
//     bought from the curve), x_total >= vx — the real reserves xr are
//     non-negative by construction, and the worst-case sell (the whole
//     circulating supply in one transaction) extracts EXACTLY xr, to
//     the floor rounding. The virtual side is mathematics, never a
//     liability.
// C2. GRADUATION = DEMAND PROOF, IN TWO CONDITIONS. A coin graduates in
//     the buy() that makes BOTH true:
//       depth:        xr >= gdx            (default 50 XEL, snapshotted)
//       continuity:  xr * y0 >= yr * vx   (structural, hard-coded)
//     The continuity condition means the pool will open at xr/yr >=
//     spot price — along the constant-k trajectory it reduces to
//     xr >= (sqrt(2)-1) * vx (~41.4 XEL at the default vx), so with the
//     defaults the depth floor binds and graduation lands around
//     2/3 of the supply sold, ~3x the launch FDV. Both conditions are
//     evaluated on the state AFTER the triggering buy (the buyer's
//     trade always completes first — VaultLaunch's exact pattern).
//     Graduation itself moves NO funds and takes NO fee: the curve
//     keeps trading at the graduated fee (the never-trap rule — if the
//     DEX is paused, holders still have the curve) until migrate().
// C3. TWO TRACKS, ONE DEX LINEAGE. VaultLaunch (projects) migrates via
//     create_pool (chunk 6, pinned to one signer — the launchpad's
//     migration driver); CommunityLaunch migrates via create_pool_open
//     (chunk 33, permissionless). A single LaunchDEX v1.4 deployment
//     can serve both (set its launchpad pin to the moderation wallet —
//     it gates set_pool_buys_paused only). The factory keeps its own
//     listing indexes (latest, by-status, migrated) and the asset ->
//     coin reverse bridge; the site never needs an indexer.
// C4. THE MIGRATION FEE IS CARVED FROM THE SEED, NOT THE CURVE. VaultLaunch
//     takes its migration fee from the reserves at graduation; here the
//     fee is taken inside migrate(), after the curve is done forever —
//     because IC3/IC4's solvency proof requires k to stay EXACTLY
//     invariant while the curve trades. (Taking it from the live curve
//     would shrink k by up to mgf and make the last sliver of a full
//     sell-back unpayable — a trap this design refuses.) The fee
//     therefore only reduces the POOL SEED, and the pool opens at the
//     real ratio the market actually paid for.
// C5. CREATOR ALLOCATION: SMALL, OFF-CURVE, POST-MIGRATION ONLY. The
//     creator declares up to 5% at launch (cap enforced, 4x tighter
//     than the project track). The allocation is EXCLUDED from the
//     curve inventory (y0 is net of it — the formula can never sell
//     it), held by the contract, and claimable ONLY once the coin has
//     migrated. A creator's payoff is conditional on graduation — the
//     alignment pump.fun made culture, written into the state machine.
//     No vesting on this track (the serious track has it); the claim
//     pays the creator's own reserve via a confidential transfer and
//     the event carries NO amount (D18 privacy, same rule).
// C6. PERMISSIONLESS MIGRATION, BOTH SIDES. migrate(cid) is callable by
//     ANYONE (the outcome is fully determined by the coin's state — no
//     destination, no amount, no caller choice anywhere), and the DEX
//     endpoint it drives (create_pool_open) is permissionless too. A
//     frontend button, a keeper bot, or the last buyer executes it in
//     the same block as graduation — no pinned wallet can become a
//     bottleneck, and an emergency-paused DEX only DELAYS the move (the
//     curve keeps trading; nothing is ever stuck).
// C7. SELLS ARE NEVER BLOCKABLE. The pause gates launch_coin and buy
//     (new XEL in) ONLY. Sells, creator claims and migration carry NO
//     pause check — exactly the launchpad's D4 and the DEX's IX6, for
//     the same reason: a pause must never become a trap.
// C8. SNAPSHOT THE RULES AT LAUNCH (the launchpad's D7, applied here):
//     the virtual reserve (vx) and the graduation depth (gdx) a coin
//     launches with are the ones it graduates by — later admin tuning
//     never reclassifies an existing coin. The fee schedule (cfe/gfe)
//     stays global, like the launchpad's.
// C9. HONEST CAPACITY: MAX_COINS (8192) bounds storage growth and the
//     static loop bounds of the listing views (R8-clean, same rule as
//     every active contract).
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIFECYCLE
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   launch_coin() [fee + asset budget attached]
//        |
//        v  Asset::create — the REAL confidential asset is born:
//        |    Fixed supply, whole balance held by the contract, cap forever.
//        |    The chain's creation cost is measured by balance-delta and
//        |    the unused part of the deposit is refunded on the spot.
//        |
//   0 LIVE (bonding with virtual reserves; buys/sells open, fee cfe)
//        |
//        |  the buy() that crosses: xr >= gdx  AND  xr*y0 >= yr*vx
//        v
//   1 GRADUATED (curve keeps trading at the graduated fee gfe; creator
//        |         allocation unlocks AT MIGRATION; no fee taken here — C4)
//        |  migrate() — permissionless, atomic (C6): mgf carved from the
//        |  seed, then ONE cross-contract call to LaunchDEX
//        |  create_pool_open (chunk 33) carrying xr + yr as deposits
//        v
//   2 MIGRATED (curve closed forever; the pool owns the market; the
//               factory keeps the coin's home — metadata, creator claim)
//
// Status codes (get_status_label): 0 live, 1 graduated, 2 migrated.
// Who triggers what: XELIS has no timers — graduation fires inside the
// buy() that crosses the conditions; migration is executed by anyone
// (frontend, keeper, buyer); everything else is a direct call.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CURVE MATH (virtual reserves, integer-exact)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   buy with D XEL attached:  fee = D * cfe / 10000        (extracted)
//                            net = D - fee                 (joins xr)
//                            out  = (yr+y0) * net / ((xr+vx) + net)  (floored)
//                            require(out <= yr)            — the whale guard
//   sell of T tokens:        gross = (xr+vx) * T / ((yr+y0) + T)     (floored)
//                            require(gross <= xr)          — provably true,
//                            fee = gross * fee / 10000      kept as belt
//                            out  = gross - fee             (to the seller)
//
//   Both floors favour the curve; all intermediates in u128 (products
//   up to ~2e31). The implied k = (xr+vx)*(yr+y0) NEVER DECREASES
//   through trades, and the migration fee never touches it (C4) — the
//   full solvency chain is IC3/IC4 below.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECURITY MODEL (honest threat documentation)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   * The admin is a hot role: it sets every fee/parameter (all
//     hard-capped), pins the DEX (before the first migration only) and
//     can pause NEW launches and NEW buys. It can NEVER: touch a
//     curve's reserves, block a sell, block a creator claim, block a
//     migration, or change a coin's state by hand (no admin entry
//     writes a c:{id}:st slot).
//   * Fees accrue to pending_fees and leave ONLY through withdraw_fees,
//     double-capped by the accrued amount and by the uncommitted
//     balance (live curve reserves are always covered first).
//   * Front-running is an assumed ceiling, like everywhere on this
//     chain: public mempool, min_out slippage protection on both
//     trade entries, no MEV protection claimed.
//   * A degenerate monster buy CAN drain a coin's whole curve inventory
//     (out == yr exactly) — such a coin graduates and simply cannot
//     migrate until a sell re-fills the inventory ("empty"): no funds
//     are at risk, the curve stays open, the state is honest.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INVARIANTS (machine-checked by tests/test_community_reference.py)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// IC1. XEL SOLVENCY, EXACT-SUM MODEL. The contract's XEL balance equals
//      the sum of every live coin's curve reserves (tcx) plus
//      pending_fees, at every block: deposits arrive whole, buys add
//      their net to xr/tcx, sells subtract their gross, migration moves
//      xr out in one atomic step (fee included), and withdraw_fees is
//      double-capped (accrued AND balance - tcx). The admin can never
//      make the factory insolvent.
// IC2. ASSET SOLVENCY, PER COIN. For every coin: the factory's balance
//      of the coin's asset equals its curve inventory (yr) plus the
//      unclaimed creator allocation — degenerating to the reserve alone
//      after migration (yr = 0). The creator allocation can never be
//      oversold (y0 is net of it at birth) and is paid exactly once.
// IC3. THE VIRTUAL PAIR NEVER LEAKS. Through trades, the product
//      k = (xr+vx)*(yr+y0) never decreases: buy floors (out floored)
//      and sell floors (gross floored) both favour the curve, and fees
//      are EXTRACTED to pending_fees, never parked in the reserves.
//      With nothing sold back, y_total <= 2*y0 forever (nothing
//      circulates that was not bought from the curve), so
//      x_total = k/y_total >= k0/(2*y0) = vx — the REAL reserves
//      xr = x_total - vx are non-negative BY CONSTRUCTION. The virtual
//      XEL can never be asked to pay a seller.
// IC4. THE WORST-CASE SELL IS EXACTLY COVERED. Selling the ENTIRE
//      circulating supply in one transaction extracts
//      vx*(y0-yr)/(y0+yr) <= xr = vx*(y0-yr)/y0 — floored to strict
//      inequality by integer rounding. The require(gross <= xr) guard
//      in sell is therefore structurally unreachable (kept so the
//      invariant is LOCAL and machine-checkable — the "fiterr" house
//      style). The whale guard on buys (out <= yr) is the same argument
//      on the token side: the virtual token reserve is mathematics,
//      never tokens.
// IC5. THE CREATOR ALLOCATION IS PAID EXACTLY ONCE. creator_remaining =
//      alloc - paid is debited atomically by claim_creator_allocation
//      (paid only ever grows, bounded by alloc); claims are
//      creator-only and gated on MIGRATED. A rejected nothing (there is
//      no rejection on this track) — but a never-graduating coin pays
//      the creator NOTHING, forever.
// IC6. STATES ONLY MOVE FORWARD, BY THE RULES. LIVE -> GRADUATED fires
//      only inside buy() when BOTH graduation conditions hold on the
//      post-trade state; GRADUATED -> MIGRATED fires only inside
//      migrate() (permissionless, deterministic). No admin entry writes
//      a coin's status, reserves or inventory. The curve never trades
//      after MIGRATED ("migrated" refusal); sells are never blocked in
//      any state that trades (C7).
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STORAGE MAP (string keys, flat KV — house style)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   Global  : adm pc sub abd cfe gfe mgf gdx vxs dxa pfe pz xa
//             tbv tsv ttc tvl mgc tcx (see constants below)
//   Coin    : c:{id}:cr creator          c:{id}:st status (0/1/2)
//             c:{id}:nm name             c:{id}:sy symbol
//             c:{id}:ds description      c:{id}:ws website
//             c:{id}:lg logo             c:{id}:tw twitter
//             c:{id}:tg telegram         c:{id}:dc discord
//             c:{id}:ts total supply     c:{id}:cb creator bps
//             c:{id}:xr real XEL res.    c:{id}:yr real tok inventory
//             c:{id}:y0 initial inventory (virtual tok reserve)
//             c:{id}:vx virtual XEL (snapshot)  c:{id}:gx grad depth (snap)
//             c:{id}:ct created topo     c:{id}:gr graduated flag
//             c:{id}:gt graduated topo   c:{id}:mi migrated flag
//             c:{id}:ma migrated topo    c:{id}:mx migrated XEL
//             c:{id}:mt migrated tokens  c:{id}:cp creator paid
//             c:{id}:ah asset hash       c:{id}:bv buy volume (XEL)
//             c:{id}:sv sell volume (XEL) c:{id}:tc trade count
//             c:{id}:lt last trade topo  c:{id}:vo total volume
//   Index   : t:{symbol} -> cid (ticker registry, one per symbol forever)
//             a:{asset_hex} -> cid (the reverse bridge, written at launch)
//             m:{order} -> cid (the migrated index, written once per move)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVENTS (V6 contract events: id + array of string fields)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//    1 CoinLaunched      [cid, name, symbol, total_supply]
//    2 CoinBought        [cid, xel_in, tokens_out, fee]
//    3 CoinSold          [cid, tokens_in, xel_out, fee]
//    4 CoinGraduated     [cid, depth_xel, curve_tokens]
//    5 CoinMigrated      [cid, xel_seed, token_seed]
//    6 CreatorClaimed    [cid]                      (NO amount — D18)
//    7 ParamSet          [param, value]
//    8 Paused            ["admin"]    9 Unpaused    ["admin"]
//   10 AdminSet          [new_admin] 11 DexSet      [dex]
//   12 CoinInfoUpdated   [cid]
//   13 MigrationFee      [cid, fee]
//   14 AssetCreated      [cid, asset_hex, fee_paid]
//   15 FeesWithdrawn     [amount]
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CHUNK TABLE (entry-point IDs, 0-based, declaration order — CI-checked)
//     0   constructor          1   only_admin           2   require_coin
//     3   coin_key             4   fee_take            5   checked_add
//     6   creator_alloc_of     7   buy_tokens_out      8   sell_xel_out
//     9   current_fee_bps     10   creator_remaining  11   record_trade
//    12   graduate_coin       13   create_coin_asset   14   migrate_coin_to_dex
//    15   launch_coin         16   buy                17   sell
//    18   migrate             19   claim_creator_allocation
//    20   update_coin_info    21   set_submission_fee  22   set_asset_budget
//    23   set_curve_fee       24   set_graduated_fee   25   set_migration_fee
//    26   set_graduation_depth 27 set_virtual_xel     28   set_dex_address
//    29   set_admin           30   set_paused         31   withdraw_fees
//    32   get_coin            33   get_coin_meta       34   get_coin_tokenomics
//    35   get_curve_info      36   get_current_price   37   get_buy_quote
//    38   get_sell_quote      39   get_market_cap      40   get_total_coins
//    41   get_coins_by_status 42   get_coin_by_rank    43   get_latest_coin
//    44   get_coin_by_asset   45   get_migrated_count  46   get_migrated_by_rank
//    47   get_trading_stats   48   get_config          49   get_status_label
//    50   get_version
//
//   PINNED FOR CROSS-CONTRACT CALLS (see LaunchDEX constants):
//     chunk 33 = create_pool_open (this factory's migrate — the OPEN
//                seeding endpoint, permissionless by design X13)
//   tests/test_community_reference.py asserts this table against the
//   source AND asserts the pinned constant against LaunchDEX's real
//   declaration order — renumbering either side without the other fails
//   CI. New functions append at the END only.
// ============================================================================

const VERSION: string = "CommunityLaunch v1.0.0"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Status codes (see LIFECYCLE)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const ST_LIVE: u64 = 0
const ST_GRADUATED: u64 = 1
const ST_MIGRATED: u64 = 2

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Global capacity (storage growth bound; also the static loop bound of the
// listing views — R8-clean)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MAX_COINS: u64 = 8192

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Asset parameters (real confidential assets, D13 lineage)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const TOKEN_DECIMALS: u8 = 8

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LaunchDEX cross-call pin — asserted against the DEX's real chunk table
// by tests/test_community_reference.py. DO NOT renumber one side alone.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const DEX_CREATE_POOL_OPEN_CHUNK: u16 = 33

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Defaults (atomic units, 8 decimals — 1 XEL = 100000000)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const DEFAULT_SUBMISSION_FEE: u64 = 100000000
const DEFAULT_ASSET_BUDGET: u64 = 100000000
const DEFAULT_CURVE_FEE_BPS: u64 = 100
